Cleaning a single folder of regular data
the data needs to already be merged
./ClusterCleaning <yyyymmdd>  
Example: ./ClusterCleaning 20250423

Cleaning bkg data
the data needs to already be merged and a background text file containeda list of files needs to be created
bkg files location shared/Trinity/DataAnalysis/DataTxtFiles/BackgroundSamples/RandomSampling/.Once the file is in there
call the filename without the file extention and  the file name MUST contain "bkg"
./ClusterCleaning <Filename> 
./ClusterCleaning bkg10hours or ./ClusterCleaning bkg40hours

Cleaning Muon data
This will  work from the file of muon data like the bkg data.  however muon data required the Forced Branch to gather data

call the  muon cleaning with 

./ClusterCleaning muon20241011


rootcling -f EventInfoDict.cpp -c EventInfo.h LinkDef.h  remake the dictionary 



